// Field table for the savestate static-data snapshot: one row per captured decomp static. Both directions
// (BackupStaticData / LoadStaticData in savestates.cpp) expand this single list, so save and load can no longer
// drift -- a row present on one side but not the other used to be a silent "saved but never restored" bug.
// SS_SCALAR(member, global) = a plain assignable; SS_BLOCK(member, global) = an array/struct (memcpy, sized by
// the snapshot member, since some live globals are incomplete-array externs). Add a captured static by adding
// its row here plus the matching `_copy` member in SaveStateInfo.

